            <div xml:id="d862">

                <pb facs="0796" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14660.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-26T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1915—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>584. Your 380, March 2, midnight. Silliman reports Carranza in reply admits no
                    responsibility. Obregon upheld. Liability for distress Mexico City denied.
                    Criticizes conduct French and German consuls and yourself. Strikers and laborers
                    eulogized. Clergy criticised without allusion to restitution. Railway
                    communication with Mexico City subject military operations through traffic
                    inadmissible while capital in enemy’s hands.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
